    "updated_at": "2020-04-12T02:10:25Z",
    "body": "Oh wow, that's happening on Zesty?\r\n\r\nI didn't realize our dynamically linked binaries were depending on libssl 1.1 now. That's a fairly new change in terms of it actually showing up in package managers, and a lot of perfectly fine systems won't be supporting that.\r\n\r\n@acornejo A question for you: would you (or I suppose anyone you know) have objected if the script attempted to install the default linux binary, and then installed the MUSL build if the default hadn't worked?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
